  Okay, I''m at the Research Counter, time to focus. My top priority is absolutely nailing down what this research task actually *is* about. The help message is clear: read the task first, no excuses. So, the command''s ready: `/execute_action{read 1}`. Let''s see what we''re dealing with. It''s "Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration" with ID 1.


  Once I''ve got that description in front of me, I need to break it down. Understand the core problem, get a good grasp of the data, the evaluation metrics, the whole shebang. Crucially, I have to analyze those provided baselines. The table gives me two options from "System": "Combat Manual Baseline" at 0.5895 and "BBKNN Manual Baseline" at 0.4138. "Combat" looks to be the current SOTA. After digging into this, I''ll probably need to look at the code of these baselines. This will give me a proper starting point.


