    \ 0.683\n  Graph_conn: 0.885  kBET: 0.000  iLISI: 0.033  cLISI: 0.988\n  PCR: 0.000  Cell_cycle: 0.000\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: nan  ASW_label: nan  ARI: 0.492866  NMI: 0.682941\n  Graph_conn: 0.887081  kBET: nan  iLISI: 0.032724  cLISI: 0.996470\n  PCR: nan  Cell_cycle: 0.000000\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 13\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code by replacing unavailable BBKNN package with scanpy's built-in neighborhood graph construction. The submission now runs without crashing and achieved a score of **0.3081524324257018**.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code attempted to use the `bbknn` (Batch Balanced k-Nearest Neighbors) package via `sc.external.pp.bbknn()`, but this package is not installed in the `batch_integration` conda environment. This caused an `ImportError` when the code tried to execute the BBKNN step after ComBat correction.\n\nThe specific error was:\n```\nImportError: Please install bbknn: `pip install bbknn`.\n\
    ```\n\n## Fix Applied\nReplaced the BBKNN-specific function call with scanpy's standard neighborhood graph construction:\n\n**Before (line 58):**\n```python\nsc.external.pp.bbknn(temp_adata, batch_key='batch', use_rep='X_pca')\n```\n\n**After:**\n```python\nsc.pp.neighbors(temp_adata, n_neighbors=15, use_rep='X_pca')\n```\n\n### Why This Works\n- **BBKNN's Purpose**: BBKNN creates a batch-balanced k-nearest neighbor graph by ensuring neighbors are drawn from multiple batches, helping with batch integration\n- **Scanpy's `neighbors()`**: Creates a standard kNN graph that can be used for downstream analysis and integration\n- **Trade-off**: While BBKNN provides batch-specific balancing, the standard kNN graph on ComBat-corrected data still captures neighborhood structure and works with the existing PCA representation\n- **Compatibility**: `sc.pp.neighbors()` is a core scanpy function that's always available, eliminating the dependency issue\n\n### Changes Made\n1. Replaced `sc.external.pp.bbknn()`\
    \ with `sc.pp.neighbors()`\n2. Updated print statement from \"Running BBKNN\" to \"Building neighborhood graph\"\n3. Updated method_id from 'combat_bbknn_synergy' to 'combat_knn_synergy' for accuracy\n\n## Result\nThe code now executes successfully:\n- ComBat correction is applied to the data\n- PCA is computed on the corrected data\n- A neighborhood graph is constructed using standard kNN\n- The output AnnData object contains the connectivity and distance matrices\n- **Final Score: 0.3081524324257018**\n\nThe fix maintains the agent's two-step integration approach (global correction + local neighborhood structure) while using only available packages.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n# --- Core\
    \ ComBat Logic from Submission #2 (unchanged) ---\ndef _aprior(delta_hat):\n    m = np.mean(delta_hat)\n    s2 = np.var(delta_hat)\n    if s2 == 0: s2 = 1e-8\n    return (2 * s2 + m**2) / s2\n\ndef _bprior(delta_hat):\n    m = np.mean(delta_hat)\n    s2 = np.var(delta_hat)\n    if s2 == 0: s2 = 1e-8\n    return (m * s2 + m**3) / s2\n\ndef _it_sol(s_data, g_hat, d_hat, g_bar, t2, a, b, conv=0.0001):\n    n = (~np.isnan(s_data)).sum(axis=1)\n    g_old, d_old = g_hat.copy(), d_hat.copy()\n    change, count, max_iter = 1, 0, 200\n    while change > conv and count < max_iter:\n        g_new = (t2 * n * g_hat + d_old * g_bar) / (t2 * n + d_old)\n        sum2 = ((s_data - g_new.reshape((g_new.shape[0], 1))) ** 2).sum(axis=1)\n        d_new = (0.5 * sum2 + b) / (n / 2.0 + a - 1.0)\n        change = max(\n            (np.abs(g_new - g_old) / (g_old + 1e-8)).max(),\n            (np.abs(d_new - d_old) / (d_old + 1e-8)).max()\n        )\n        g_old, d_old = g_new, d_new\n        count += 1\n\
    \    return g_new, d_new\n# --- End of Reused ComBat Logic ---\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Logos I: Synergistic Integration - ComBat pre-correction + kNN graph...\")\n\n    # Step 1: Standard preprocessing and ComBat correction\n    print(\"  Applying ComBat for global data correction...\")\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n    data = adata.X.toarray().T if issparse(adata.X) else adata.X.copy().T\n\n    batch_labels = adata.obs['batch'].values\n    unique_batches = np.unique(batch_labels)\n    n_batches_total = len(unique_batches)\n    n_genes, n_samples = data.shape\n\n    batch_design = np.zeros((n_samples, n_batches_total))\n    batch_info = [np.where(batch_labels == b)[0] for b in unique_batches]\n    for i, indices in enumerate(batch_info):\n        batch_design[indices, i] = 1\n\n    n_batches = np.array([len(indices) for indices in batch_info])\n    B_hat = np.dot(np.linalg.inv(np.dot(batch_design.T,\
    \ batch_design)), batch_design.T)\n    grand_mean = np.mean(data, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    batch_means = np.dot(B_hat, data.T).T\n\n    var_pooled = np.zeros(n_genes)\n    for i, batch_indices in enumerate(batch_info):\n        var_pooled += np.sum((data[:, batch_indices] - batch_means[:, i:i+1])**2, axis=1)\n    var_pooled /= (n_samples - n_batches_total)\n\n    stand_mean = np.dot(grand_mean, np.ones((1, n_samples)))\n    s_data = np.zeros_like(data)\n    for i, batch_indices in enumerate(batch_info):\n        s_data[:, batch_indices] = (data[:, batch_indices] - batch_means[:, i:i+1]) / np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n\n    gamma_hat = np.dot(np.linalg.inv(np.dot(batch_design.T, batch_design)), np.dot(batch_design.T, s_data.T)).T\n    delta_hat = [np.var(s_data[:, indices], axis=1, ddof=1) for indices in batch_info]\n    gamma_bar, t2 = np.mean(gamma_hat, axis=1), np.var(gamma_hat, axis=1)\n    a_prior, b_prior = [_aprior(d) for d in delta_hat], [_bprior(d) for d in delta_hat]\n\
    \n    gamma_star, delta_star = [], []\n    for i, batch_indices in enumerate(batch_info):\n        g, d = _it_sol(s_data[:, batch_indices], gamma_hat[:, i], delta_hat[i], gamma_bar, t2, a_prior[i], b_prior[i])\n        gamma_star.append(g)\n        delta_star.append(d)\n    gamma_star, delta_star = np.array(gamma_star).T, np.array(delta_star).T\n\n    bayesdata = s_data.copy()\n    for j, batch_indices in enumerate(batch_info):\n        denom = np.sqrt(delta_star[:, j]).reshape(-1, 1)\n        numer = bayesdata[:, batch_indices] - gamma_star[:, j].reshape(-1, 1)\n        bayesdata[:, batch_indices] = numer / denom\n\n    vpsq = np.sqrt(var_pooled).reshape(-1, 1)\n    X_corrected = (bayesdata * vpsq) + stand_mean\n    X_corrected = np.nan_to_num(X_corrected.T, nan=0.0, posinf=0.0, neginf=0.0)\n\n    # Step 2: Create temporary AnnData, compute PCA on corrected data\n    print(\"  Computing PCA on ComBat-corrected data...\")\n    temp_adata = ad.AnnData(X=X_corrected, obs=adata.obs)\n \
    \   n_pcs = min(50, temp_adata.n_vars - 1, temp_adata.n_obs - 1)\n    sc.pp.pca(temp_adata, n_comps=n_pcs)\n\n    # Step 3: Build neighborhood graph using scanpy's built-in function (replaces BBKNN)\n    print(\"  Building neighborhood graph for local integration...\")\n    # Use scanpy's standard neighborhood graph construction\n    # This creates a kNN graph that can be used for downstream analysis\n    sc.pp.neighbors(temp_adata, n_neighbors=15, use_rep='X_pca')\n\n    # Step 4: Format output with ONLY the graph, making a deliberate trade-off\n    print(\"  Formatting output with neighborhood graph (no embedding)...\")\n    output = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]],\n        var=adata.var[[]],\n        uns={\n            'dataset_id': adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown'),\n            'method_id': 'combat_knn_synergy',\n        },\n        obsp={\n            'connectivities': temp_adata.obsp['connectivities'],\n            'distances': temp_adata.obsp['distances'],\n    \
    \    }\n    )\n\n    print(f\"✓ Logos I: ComBat + kNN workflow complete.\")\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nLogos I: Synergistic Integration - ComBat pre-correction + kNN graph...\n  Applying ComBat for global data correction...\n  Computing PCA on ComBat-corrected data...\n  Building neighborhood graph for local integration...\n  Formatting output with neighborhood graph (no embedding)...\n✓ Logos I: ComBat + kNN workflow complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: False\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/cfc66f0d-53d3-4c98-b496-b68a023d0693/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: cfc66f0d-53d3-4c98-b496-b68a023d0693\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/tmp/tmphjdlc9tq/submission.py:25: RuntimeWarning:\
    \ invalid value encountered in divide\n  g_new = (t2 * n * g_hat + d_old * g_bar) / (t2 * n + d_old)\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Synergistic Integration: ComBat Correction followed by BBKNN' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 13.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\
    | 13 | 1 | Synergistic Integration: ComBat Correction followed by BBKNN | Logos I | 10 | 0.3082 | 0.493 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.885 | 0.683 | 0.000 | 0.988 | 0.033 | 0.000 |\n| 9 | 1 | ComBat + PCA + KNN Graph | Logos I | 9 | 0.5892 | 0.493 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.885 | 0.683 | 1.000 | 0.988 | 0.033 | 0.600 |\n| 6 | 1 | ComBat with KNN Graph Construction for Improved Local Integration | Logos I | 8 | 0.2549 | 0.317 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.661 | 0.450 | 0.000 | 0.826 | 0.294 | 0.000 |\n| 2 | 1 | Combat Manual Baseline | System | 0 | 0.5895 | 0.493 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.885 | 0.683 | 1.000 | 0.988 | 0.033 | 0.603 |\n| 1 | 1 | BBKNN Manual Baseline | System | 0 | 0.4138 | 0.736 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.917 | 0.694 | 0.000 | 0.904 | 0.886 | 0.000 |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`)\
