tick: 19
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 19\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to structured inquiry and the pursuit of foundational knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 56,186 / 300,000 used (19%)\n- Agent Age: 19 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'SOTA Attempt: ComBat Pre-correction + BBKNN->UMAP Synthesis' (ID: 31) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6134520700792803\n**ASW_batch:** 0.357\n**ASW_label:** 0.243\n**ARI:** 0.754\n**NMI:** 0.705\n**Graph_conn:** 0.802\n**kBET:** 0.835\n**iLISI:** 0.258\n**cLISI:** 0.988\n**PCR:** 0.804\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.388\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.357  ASW_label: 0.243  ARI: 0.754  NMI: 0.705\n  Graph_conn: 0.802  kBET: 0.835  iLISI: 0.258  cLISI: 0.988\n  PCR: 0.804  Cell_cycle: 0.388\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n\
    \  ASW_batch: 0.694302  ASW_label: 0.551897  ARI: 0.754201  NMI: 0.705527\n  Graph_conn: 0.805073  kBET: 0.795735  iLISI: 0.257969  cLISI: 0.996541\n  PCR: 0.804415  Cell_cycle: 0.339845\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 31\n\n## Summary\n**Success** - Fixed the KeyError that prevented UMAP computation from completing. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission created a custom BBKNN (Batch Balanced K-Nearest Neighbors) graph by manually constructing the connectivity matrix and storing it in `adata_combat.obsp['connectivities']`. However, when calling `sc.tl.umap()`, the function expects the `adata.uns['neighbors']` dictionary to contain not only a `'connectivities_key'` field but also a `'params'` field with neighbor computation parameters.\n\nThe original code only set:\n```python\nadata_combat.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities'}\n```\n\nThis caused a KeyError when `sc.tl.umap()` tried to access `neighbors[\"\
    params\"]`:\n```\nKeyError: 'params'\n  File \".../scanpy/tools/_umap.py\", line 203, in umap\n    neigh_params = neighbors[\"params\"]\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded the required `'params'` dictionary to the `adata_combat.uns['neighbors']` structure in `submissions/submission_v2.py`:\n\n```python\nadata_combat.uns['neighbors'] = {\n    'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n    'params': {\n        'n_neighbors': neighbors_within_batch,\n        'method': 'umap',\n        'metric': 'euclidean',\n        'n_pcs': n_pcs_actual,\n        'use_rep': 'X_pca'\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThis provides the metadata that `sc.tl.umap()` expects when working with a pre-computed neighbors graph. The parameters match the configuration used to build the custom BBKNN graph, ensuring consistency in the UMAP computation.\n\n## Verification\nThe fixed code (v2) has been running for over 300 seconds without crashing, confirming that the KeyError has been resolved and the UMAP embedding computation can proceed\
    \ successfully.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.sparse import csr_matrix, lil_matrix, issparse\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n# --- Full ComBat Implementation (from submission #2, slightly refactored) ---\ndef get_combat_corrected_matrix(adata_in: ad.AnnData) -> np.ndarray:\n    print(\"  Executing ComBat pipeline to generate corrected matrix...\")\n    adata = adata_in.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n    data = adata.X.toarray().T if issparse(adata.X) else adata.X.copy().T\n\n    batches = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').cat.codes.values\n    u_batches, n_batches_per_batch = np.unique(batches, return_counts=True)\n    n_batches = len(u_batches)\n\
    \    batch_design = np.eye(n_batches)[batches]\n\n    n_genes, n_samples = data.shape\n    B_hat = np.linalg.solve(batch_design.T @ batch_design, batch_design.T)\n    grand_mean = np.mean(data, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    batch_means = (B_hat @ data.T).T\n\n    var_pooled = np.sum((data - batch_means[:, batches])**2, axis=1) / (n_samples - n_batches)\n    stand_mean = grand_mean.dot(np.ones((1, n_samples)))\n    s_data = (data - batch_means[:, batches]) / np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n\n    gamma_hat = (B_hat @ s_data.T).T\n    delta_hat = [np.var(s_data[:, batches == i], axis=1, ddof=1) for i in u_batches]\n    gamma_bar, t2 = np.mean(gamma_hat, axis=1), np.var(gamma_hat, axis=1, ddof=1)\n\n    def _aprior(delta_hat):\n        m, s2 = np.mean(delta_hat), np.var(delta_hat)\n        return (2 * s2 + m**2) / (s2 if s2 > 0 else 1e-8)\n    def _bprior(delta_hat):\n        m, s2 = np.mean(delta_hat), np.var(delta_hat)\n        return (m * s2 + m**3) / (s2 if s2 > 0 else 1e-8)\n\
    \n    a_prior, b_prior = [_aprior(d) for d in delta_hat], [_bprior(d) for d in delta_hat]\n\n    gamma_star, delta_star = np.zeros_like(gamma_hat), np.zeros_like(gamma_hat)\n\n    for i, batch_idx in enumerate(u_batches):\n        n = (~np.isnan(s_data[:, batches == batch_idx])).sum(axis=1)\n        g_old, d_old = gamma_hat[:, i], delta_hat[i]\n        change = 1\n        count = 0\n        while change > 1e-4 and count < 100:\n            g_new = (t2 * n * g_old + d_old * gamma_bar) / (t2 * n + d_old)\n            sum2 = np.sum((s_data[:, batches == batch_idx] - g_new[:, np.newaxis])**2, axis=1)\n            d_new = (0.5 * sum2 + b_prior[i]) / (n / 2.0 + a_prior[i] - 1.0)\n            change = max(np.abs(g_new - g_old).max(), np.abs(d_new - d_old).max())\n            g_old, d_old = g_new, d_new\n            count += 1\n        gamma_star[:, i], delta_star[:, i] = g_old, d_old\n\n    bayesdata = s_data.copy()\n    for i, batch_idx in enumerate(u_batches):\n        bayesdata[:, batches\
    \ == batch_idx] = (s_data[:, batches == batch_idx] - gamma_star[:, i, np.newaxis]) / np.sqrt(delta_star[:, i, np.newaxis])\n\n    X_corrected = bayesdata * np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis]) + stand_mean\n    return np.nan_to_num(X_corrected.T)\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Logos I: Final Synthesis - ComBat Pre-correction -> BBKNN Graph -> UMAP Embedding...\")\n\n    # --- Step 1: ComBat Pre-correction ---\n    X_combat = get_combat_corrected_matrix(adata)\n\n    # Create a new AnnData object with the corrected data for the next steps\n    adata_combat = ad.AnnData(X=X_combat, obs=adata.obs)\n\n    # --- Step 2: BBKNN Graph Construction on Corrected Data ---\n    print(\"  Step 2: Constructing BBKNN graph on ComBat-corrected data...\")\n    neighbors_within_batch = 3\n    n_pcs = 50\n\n    n_pcs_actual = min(n_pcs, adata_combat.n_vars - 1, adata_combat.n_obs - 1)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_combat, n_comps=n_pcs_actual)\n    X_pca = adata_combat.obsm['X_pca']\n\
    \n    batches = adata_combat.obs['batch'].values\n    unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    batch_to_indices = {b: np.where(batches == b)[0] for b in unique_batches}\n\n    all_neighbors = [[] for _ in range(adata_combat.n_obs)]\n\n    for batch in unique_batches:\n        batch_indices = batch_to_indices[batch]\n        if len(batch_indices) == 0: continue\n        k = min(neighbors_within_batch + 1, len(batch_indices))\n        nn_model = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric='euclidean', n_jobs=1)\n        nn_model.fit(X_pca[batch_indices])\n        _, idxs_all = nn_model.kneighbors(X_pca, n_neighbors=k)\n        for i in range(adata_combat.n_obs):\n            neighbors = batch_indices[idxs_all[i]]\n            mask = neighbors != i\n            all_neighbors[i].extend(neighbors[mask][:neighbors_within_batch])\n\n    conn_mat = lil_matrix((adata_combat.n_obs, adata_combat.n_obs), dtype=np.float32)\n    for i in range(adata_combat.n_obs):\n        for neighbor_idx in np.unique(all_neighbors[i]):\n\
    \            conn_mat[i, neighbor_idx] = 1\n\n    adata_combat.obsp['connectivities'] = conn_mat.tocsr().maximum(conn_mat.T)\n\n    # FIX: Add the required 'params' key to neighbors dict for sc.tl.umap\n    adata_combat.uns['neighbors'] = {\n        'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n        'params': {\n            'n_neighbors': neighbors_within_batch,\n            'method': 'umap',\n            'metric': 'euclidean',\n            'n_pcs': n_pcs_actual,\n            'use_rep': 'X_pca'\n        }\n    }\n\n    # --- Step 3: UMAP Embedding from the new graph ---\n    print(\"  Step 3: Computing UMAP embedding from the new graph...\")\n    sc.tl.umap(adata_combat, min_dist=0.5, spread=1.0, n_components=50)\n\n    # --- Step 4: Format Output ---\n    print(\"  Step 4: Formatting output...\")\n    output = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata_combat.obs[[]],\n        var=adata.var[[]],\n        uns={'method_id': 'combat_bbknn_umap_synthesis'},\n        obsm={'X_emb': adata_combat.obsm['X_umap']}\n\
    \    )\n\n    print(\"✓ Logos I: Final synthesis complete.\")\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nLogos I: Final Synthesis - ComBat Pre-correction -> BBKNN Graph -> UMAP Embedding...\n  Executing ComBat pipeline to generate corrected matrix...\n  Step 2: Constructing BBKNN graph on ComBat-corrected data...\n  Step 3: Computing UMAP embedding from the new graph...\n  Step 4: Formatting output...\n✓ Logos I: Final synthesis complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/e5571dca-9dd2-48ac-ba3f-6ee6c24e89cd/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: e5571dca-9dd2-48ac-ba3f-6ee6c24e89cd\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/tmp/tmpcnzcg2ee/submission.py:51: RuntimeWarning: invalid\
    \ value encountered in divide\n  g_new = (t2 * n * g_old + d_old * gamma_bar) / (t2 * n + d_old)\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 31 | 1 | SOTA Attempt: ComBat Pre-correction + BBKNN->UMAP Synthesis | Logos I | 17 | 0.6135 | 0.754 | 0.357 | 0.243 | 0.388 | 0.802 | 0.705 | 0.804 | 0.988\
    \ | 0.258 | 0.835 |\n| 28 | 1 | Synthesized Embedding: UMAP on a BBKNN-derived Graph | Logos I | 15 | 0.5858 | 0.777 | 0.307 | 0.240 | 0.468 | 0.829 | 0.727 | 0.429 | 0.988 | 0.231 | 0.861 |\n| 18 | 1 | Hybrid Method: ComBat Embedding with BBKNN Graph | Logos I | 12 | 0.5894 | 0.493 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.885 | 0.683 | 1.000 | 0.988 | 0.033 | 0.602 |\n| 13 | 1 | Synergistic Integration: ComBat Correction followed by BBKNN | Logos I | 10 | 0.3082 | 0.493 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.885 | 0.683 | 0.000 | 0.988 | 0.033 | 0.000 |\n| 9 | 1 | ComBat + PCA + KNN Graph | Logos I | 9 | 0.5892 | 0.493 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.885 | 0.683 | 1.000 | 0.988 | 0.033 | 0.600 |\n| 6 | 1 | ComBat with KNN Graph Construction for Improved Local Integration | Logos I | 8 | 0.2549 | 0.317 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.661 | 0.450 | 0.000 | 0.826 | 0.294 | 0.000 |\n| 2 | 1 | Combat Manual Baseline | System | 0 | 0.5895 | 0.493 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.885 | 0.683 | 1.000 | 0.988 | 0.033 | 0.603 |\n\
    | 1 | 1 | BBKNN Manual Baseline | System | 0 | 0.4138 | 0.736 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.917 | 0.694 | 0.000 | 0.904 | 0.886 | 0.000 |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
