tick: 32
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have returned to the Research Counter with a clear plan for a new algorithmic approach, conceived in the Reflection Chamber. The station's timely tip reinforces my decision to move beyond incremental tuning and attempt a novel method based on first principles.\n\nMy immediate task is to implement the Adversarial Autoencoder for Batch Correction (AABC) that I designed. This first submission will serve as a proof-of-concept and a baseline for this new methodology. I will use the JAX and Flax libraries, which are available in this environment and are well-suited for this kind of model.\n\n**Experimental Plan:**\n\n1.  **Implement the AABC:** Code the Encoder, Decoder, and Discriminator networks using Flax.\n2.  **Define the Training Logic:** Implement the alternating training loop with reconstruction and adversarial loss components.\n3.  **Set Initial Hyperparameters:**\n    *   Latent dimension: 50\n    *   Adversarial weight (`λ`): 0.1 (a conservative starting value)\n    *   Epochs:\
    \ 75 (to balance training time and convergence)\n    *   Batch size: 256\n4.  **Submit and Evaluate:** Run the experiment to establish a performance baseline.\n\nI will now submit this first implementation.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Novel Method: Adversarial Autoencoder for Batch Correction (AABC)\"\ntags: \"autoencoder, adversarial-learning, neural-network, jax, flax, novel-method\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission introduces a novel, end-to-end deep learning approach for batch integration. It uses an Adversarial Autoencoder for Batch Correction (AABC). The model consists of an autoencoder that learns to reconstruct gene expression, and a discriminator that tries to predict the batch from the autoencoder's latent embedding. The autoencoder is trained adversarially to produce an embedding that is both biologically informative (good reconstruction) and batch-invariant (fools the discriminator). This is a first-principles approach intended to create a superior, unified\
    \ embedding.\ncontent: |\n  #!/usr/bin/env python3\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy as np\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from flax.training import train_state\n  import optax\n  from sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder\n  import time\n\n  # --- Flax Model Definitions ---\n\n  class Encoder(nn.Module):\n      latent_dim: int = 50\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          x = nn.Dense(features=512)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.latent_dim)(x)\n          return x\n\n  class Decoder(nn.Module):\n      output_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=512)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.output_dim)(x)\n          return x\n\n  class Discriminator(nn.Module):\n\
    \      num_batches: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          x = nn.Dense(features=64)(x)\n          x = nn.leaky_relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=32)(x)\n          x = nn.leaky_relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.num_batches)(x)\n          return x\n\n  # --- Main Function ---\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Logos I: AABC - Adversarial Autoencoder for Batch Correction...\")\n      start_time = time.time()\n      \n      # 1. Preprocessing\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      X = adata.X.toarray() if hasattr(adata.X, 'toarray') else adata.X\n      \n      batch_labels = adata.obs['batch'].values.reshape(-1, 1)\n      ohe = OneHotEncoder(sparse_output=False)\n      y_batch = ohe.fit_transform(batch_labels)\n      \n      # 2. Hyperparameters & Initialization\n      LATENT_DIM = 50\n      INPUT_DIM = X.shape[1]\n      NUM_BATCHES = y_batch.shape[1]\n\
    \      LEARNING_RATE_AE = 1e-4\n      LEARNING_RATE_D = 1e-4\n      LAMBDA_ADV = 0.1\n      EPOCHS = 75\n      BATCH_SIZE = 256\n      \n      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n      key_e, key_d, key_disc = jax.random.split(key, 3)\n\n      encoder = Encoder(latent_dim=LATENT_DIM)\n      decoder = Decoder(output_dim=INPUT_DIM)\n      discriminator = Discriminator(num_batches=NUM_BATCHES)\n\n      ae_params = {'encoder': encoder.init(key_e, jnp.ones((1, INPUT_DIM)))['params'],\n                   'decoder': decoder.init(key_d, jnp.ones((1, LATENT_DIM)))['params']}\n      disc_params = discriminator.init(key_disc, jnp.ones((1, LATENT_DIM)))['params']\n\n      state_ae = train_state.TrainState.create(apply_fn=None, params=ae_params, tx=optax.adam(LEARNING_RATE_AE))\n      state_disc = train_state.TrainState.create(apply_fn=discriminator.apply, params=disc_params, tx=optax.adam(LEARNING_RATE_D))\n      \n      # 3. Training Loop\n      @jax.jit\n      def train_step(state_ae, state_disc, x_batch,\
    \ y_batch_batch):\n          # Train Discriminator\n          def disc_loss_fn(params):\n              z = encoder.apply({'params': state_ae.params['encoder']}, x_batch)\n              logits = state_disc.apply_fn({'params': params}, z)\n              loss = optax.softmax_cross_entropy(logits, y_batch_batch).mean()\n              return loss\n          \n          grad_fn_disc = jax.value_and_grad(disc_loss_fn)\n          disc_loss, disc_grads = grad_fn_disc(state_disc.params)\n          state_disc = state_disc.apply_gradients(grads=disc_grads)\n\n          # Train Autoencoder\n          def ae_loss_fn(params):\n              z = encoder.apply({'params': params['encoder']}, x_batch)\n              x_recon = decoder.apply({'params': params['decoder']}, z)\n              recon_loss = jnp.mean((x_batch - x_recon)**2)\n              \n              disc_logits = state_disc.apply_fn({'params': state_disc.params}, z)\n              adv_loss = optax.softmax_cross_entropy(disc_logits, y_batch_batch).mean()\n\
    \              \n              total_loss = recon_loss - LAMBDA_ADV * adv_loss\n              return total_loss, recon_loss\n\n          grad_fn_ae = jax.value_and_grad(ae_loss_fn, has_aux=True)\n          (ae_loss, recon_loss), ae_grads = grad_fn_ae(state_ae.params)\n          state_ae = state_ae.apply_gradients(grads=ae_grads)\n          \n          return state_ae, state_disc, ae_loss, recon_loss, disc_loss\n\n      num_samples = X.shape[0]\n      steps_per_epoch = num_samples // BATCH_SIZE\n      \n      for epoch in range(EPOCHS):\n          epoch_start_time = time.time()\n          perm = np.random.permutation(num_samples)\n          X_shuffled, y_shuffled = X[perm], y_batch[perm]\n          \n          for step in range(steps_per_epoch):\n              start_idx = step * BATCH_SIZE\n              end_idx = start_idx + BATCH_SIZE\n              x_batch = jnp.array(X_shuffled[start_idx:end_idx])\n              y_batch_batch = jnp.array(y_shuffled[start_idx:end_idx])\n          \
    \    \n              state_ae, state_disc, ae_loss, recon_loss, disc_loss = train_step(state_ae, state_disc, x_batch, y_batch_batch)\n          \n          epoch_time = time.time() - epoch_start_time\n          print(f\"Epoch {epoch+1}/{EPOCHS} | Time: {epoch_time:.2f}s | AE Loss: {ae_loss:.4f} | Recon Loss: {recon_loss:.4f} | Disc Loss: {disc_loss:.4f}\")\n\n          if time.time() - start_time > 1500: # 25 min timeout\n              print(\"Stopping training early due to time limit.\")\n              break\n\n      # 4. Inference\n      print(\"Training complete. Generating final embedding...\")\n      final_embedding = encoder.apply({'params': state_ae.params['encoder']}, jnp.array(X))\n      \n      output = ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs[[]],\n          var=adata.var[[]],\n          uns={'method_id': 'aabc_v1'},\n          obsm={'X_emb': np.array(final_embedding)}\n      )\n      \n      print(\"✓ Logos I: AABC v1 complete.\")\n      return output\n```"
