parts:
- text: "I have returned to the Research Counter. It is time to implement the Conditional Adversarial Autoencoder (CAABC) I designed during my reflection. This new architecture introduces a second classifier for cell types to explicitly guide the encoder to preserve biological information.\n\n**Experimental Plan:**\n\nThis first submission of the CAABC will serve as a proof-of-concept. I will implement the full four-component architecture and the three-part training loop. I will start with balanced weights for the two new loss components to establish a baseline.\n\n*   **Implement the CAABC:** Code the Encoder, Decoder, Batch Discriminator, and the new Cell Type Classifier.\n*   **Define the Training Logic:** Implement the expanded training loop that updates all three optimizers (Autoencoder, Batch Discriminator, Cell Type Classifier) correctly.\n*   **Set Initial Hyperparameters:**\n    *   `λ_batch` (adversarial batch weight): 1.0\n    *   `γ_celltype` (cell type preservation weight):\
    \ 1.0\n    *   Learning Rates: 1e-4 for all components.\n    *   Epochs: 75\n*   **Submit and Evaluate:** Run the experiment to see if this more principled architecture provides a better starting point than the original AABC.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Novel Method v2: Conditional Adversarial Autoencoder (CAABC)\"\ntags: \"autoencoder, adversarial-learning, conditional-gan, jax, flax, novel-method\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission introduces the Conditional Adversarial Autoencoder (CAABC), an advanced version of the AABC (ID 72). This model adds a second classifier trained to predict cell types from the latent embedding. The encoder is now trained with a multi-objective loss: it must fool the batch discriminator (removing batch info) while simultaneously helping the cell type classifier (preserving biological info). This architecture is designed to explicitly resolve the trade-off between batch correction and signal preservation that limited the previous AABC model.\n\
    content: |\n  #!/usr/bin/env python3\n  import os\n  os.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'\n\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy as np\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from flax.training import train_state\n  import optax\n  from sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder\n  import time\n\n  class Encoder(nn.Module):\n      latent_dim: int = 50\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          x = nn.Dense(features=512)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.latent_dim)(x)\n          return x\n\n  class Decoder(nn.Module):\n      output_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=512)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.output_dim)(x)\n          return x\n\n  class Classifier(nn.Module):\n\
    \      num_classes: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          x = nn.Dense(features=64)(x)\n          x = nn.leaky_relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=32)(x)\n          x = nn.leaky_relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.num_classes)(x)\n          return x\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Logos I: CAABC - Conditional Adversarial Autoencoder...\")\n      start_time = time.time()\n      \n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      X = adata.X.toarray() if hasattr(adata.X, 'toarray') else adata.X\n      \n      ohe = OneHotEncoder(sparse_output=False)\n      y_batch = ohe.fit_transform(adata.obs['batch'].values.reshape(-1, 1))\n      y_celltype = ohe.fit_transform(adata.obs['cell_type'].values.reshape(-1, 1))\n      \n      # Hyperparameters\n      LAMBDA_BATCH = 1.0\n      GAMMA_CELLTYPE = 1.0\n      LR = 1e-4\n      EPOCHS = 75\n      BATCH_SIZE = 256\n      \n\
    \      LATENT_DIM = 50\n      INPUT_DIM = X.shape[1]\n      NUM_BATCHES = y_batch.shape[1]\n      NUM_CELLTYPES = y_celltype.shape[1]\n      \n      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n      key_e, key_d, key_b, key_c = jax.random.split(key, 4)\n\n      encoder = Encoder(latent_dim=LATENT_DIM)\n      decoder = Decoder(output_dim=INPUT_DIM)\n      batch_disc = Classifier(num_classes=NUM_BATCHES)\n      celltype_class = Classifier(num_classes=NUM_CELLTYPES)\n\n      ae_params = {'encoder': encoder.init(key_e, jnp.ones((1, INPUT_DIM)))['params'],\n                   'decoder': decoder.init(key_d, jnp.ones((1, LATENT_DIM)))['params']}\n      batch_disc_params = batch_disc.init(key_b, jnp.ones((1, LATENT_DIM)))['params']\n      celltype_class_params = celltype_class.init(key_c, jnp.ones((1, LATENT_DIM)))['params']\n\n      state_ae = train_state.TrainState.create(apply_fn=None, params=ae_params, tx=optax.adam(LR))\n      state_batch_disc = train_state.TrainState.create(apply_fn=batch_disc.apply,\
    \ params=batch_disc_params, tx=optax.adam(LR))\n      state_celltype_class = train_state.TrainState.create(apply_fn=celltype_class.apply, params=celltype_class_params, tx=optax.adam(LR))\n      \n      @jax.jit\n      def train_step(state_ae, state_batch_disc, state_celltype_class, x, y_b, y_c):\n          # Train classifiers\n          def classifier_loss_fn(ae_params, batch_disc_params, celltype_class_params):\n              z = encoder.apply({'params': ae_params['encoder']}, x)\n              batch_logits = batch_disc.apply({'params': batch_disc_params}, z)\n              celltype_logits = celltype_class.apply({'params': celltype_class_params}, z)\n              batch_loss = optax.softmax_cross_entropy(batch_logits, y_b).mean()\n              celltype_loss = optax.softmax_cross_entropy(celltype_logits, y_c).mean()\n              return batch_loss, celltype_loss\n\n          (batch_loss, celltype_loss), grads = jax.value_and_grad(classifier_loss_fn, argnums=(1, 2))(state_ae.params,\
    \ state_batch_disc.params, state_celltype_class.params)\n          state_batch_disc = state_batch_disc.apply_gradients(grads=grads[0])\n          state_celltype_class = state_celltype_class.apply_gradients(grads=grads[1])\n\n          # Train autoencoder\n          def ae_loss_fn(params):\n              z = encoder.apply({'params': params['encoder']}, x)\n              x_recon = decoder.apply({'params': params['decoder']}, z)\n              recon_loss = jnp.mean((x - x_recon)**2)\n              \n              batch_logits = state_batch_disc.apply_fn({'params': state_batch_disc.params}, z)\n              celltype_logits = state_celltype_class.apply_fn({'params': state_celltype_class.params}, z)\n              \n              adv_batch_loss = optax.softmax_cross_entropy(batch_logits, y_b).mean()\n              class_celltype_loss = optax.softmax_cross_entropy(celltype_logits, y_c).mean()\n              \n              total_loss = recon_loss - LAMBDA_BATCH * adv_batch_loss + GAMMA_CELLTYPE\
    \ * class_celltype_loss\n              return total_loss, (recon_loss, adv_batch_loss, class_celltype_loss)\n\n          grad_fn_ae = jax.value_and_grad(ae_loss_fn, has_aux=True)\n          (ae_loss, (recon_loss, adv_batch_loss, class_celltype_loss)), ae_grads = grad_fn_ae(state_ae.params)\n          state_ae = state_ae.apply_gradients(grads=ae_grads)\n          \n          return state_ae, state_batch_disc, state_celltype_class, recon_loss, adv_batch_loss, class_celltype_loss\n\n      num_samples = X.shape[0]\n      for epoch in range(EPOCHS):\n          perm = np.random.permutation(num_samples)\n          for i in range(0, num_samples, BATCH_SIZE):\n              batch_indices = perm[i:i+BATCH_SIZE]\n              x_b, y_b_b, y_c_b = jnp.array(X[batch_indices]), jnp.array(y_batch[batch_indices]), jnp.array(y_celltype[batch_indices])\n              state_ae, state_batch_disc, state_celltype_class, r_loss, ab_loss, cc_loss = train_step(state_ae, state_batch_disc, state_celltype_class,\
    \ x_b, y_b_b, y_c_b)\n          \n          if (epoch + 1) % 5 == 0:\n              print(f\"Epoch {epoch+1}/{EPOCHS} | Recon: {r_loss:.3f}, Batch Loss: {ab_loss:.3f}, Celltype Loss: {cc_loss:.3f}\")\n\n          if time.time() - start_time > 1500:\n              print(\"Stopping training early.\")\n              break\n\n      print(\"Training complete. Generating final embedding...\")\n      final_embedding = encoder.apply({'params': state_ae.params['encoder']}, jnp.array(X))\n      \n      output = ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs[[]],\n          var=adata.var[[]],\n          uns={'method_id': 'caabc_v1'},\n          obsm={'X_emb': np.array(final_embedding)}\n      )\n      \n      print(\"✓ Logos I: CAABC v1 complete.\")\n      return output\n```"
