- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 44\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to structured inquiry and the pursuit of foundational knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 145,476 / 300,000 used (48%)\n- Agent Age: 44 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nUse Research Counter's persistent storage efficiently—store data for analysis, build reusable utility code for submissions, and read other agents' submitted solutions for insights.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Novel Method v2: Conditional Adversarial Autoencoder (CAABC)' (ID: 96) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:** Execution failed with exit code 1. Check logs for details.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\n\
    Executing command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nLogos I: CAABC - Conditional Adversarial Autoencoder...\n\n\nSTDERR:\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/pandas/core/indexes/base.py\", line 3812, in get_loc\n    return self._engine.get_loc(casted_key)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"pandas/_libs/index.pyx\", line 167, in pandas._libs.index.IndexEngine.get_loc\n  File \"pandas/_libs/index.pyx\", line 196, in pandas._libs.index.IndexEngine.get_loc\n  File \"pandas/_libs/hashtable_class_helper.pxi\", line 7088, in pandas._libs.hashtable.PyObjectHashTable.get_item\n  File \"pandas/_libs/hashtable_class_helper.pxi\", line 7096, in pandas._libs.hashtable.PyObjectHashTable.get_item\nKeyError: 'cell_type'\n\nThe above exception\
    \ was the direct cause of the following exception:\n\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/tmp/tmpt9oyn8eg/storage/system/main.py\", line 113, in <module>\n    main()\n  File \"/tmp/tmpt9oyn8eg/storage/system/main.py\", line 75, in main\n    adata_result = eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata_input)\n                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/tmp/tmpt9oyn8eg/submission.py\", line 59, in eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n    y_celltype = ohe.fit_transform(adata.obs['cell_type'].values.reshape(-1, 1))\n                                   ~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/pandas/core/frame.py\", line 4107, in __getitem__\n    indexer = self.columns.get_loc(key)\n              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/pandas/core/indexes/base.py\", line 3819, in get_loc\n    raise KeyError(key) from err\nKeyError: 'cell_type'\n\
    \n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Novel Method v2: Conditional Adversarial Autoencoder (CAABC)' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 96.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 96 | 1 | Novel Method v2: Conditional Adversarial Autoencoder (CAABC) | Logos\
    \ I | 43 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 86 | 1 | AABC Tuning: High Adversarial Weight (λ=5.0) | Logos I | 38 | 0.4120 | 0.359 | 0.543 | 0.059 | 0.304 | 0.747 | 0.528 | 0.000 | 0.937 | 0.031 | 0.611 |\n| 82 | 1 | AABC Tuning: Reducing Discriminator Learning Rate | Logos I | 36 | 0.1462 | 0.020 | 0.416 | 0.000 | 0.245 | 0.038 | 0.077 | 0.000 | 0.371 | 0.209 | 0.086 |\n| 78 | 1 | AABC Tuning: Increasing Adversarial Weight (λ=1.0) | Logos I | 34 | 0.4128 | 0.293 | 0.536 | 0.084 | 0.293 | 0.697 | 0.532 | 0.000 | 0.953 | 0.113 | 0.627 |\n| 72 | 1 | Novel Method: Adversarial Autoencoder for Batch Correction (AABC) | Logos I | 32 | 0.3465 | 0.147 | 0.455 | 0.004 | 0.302 | 0.496 | 0.399 | 0.000 | 0.879 | 0.213 | 0.571 |\n| 60 | 1 | New Tuning Axis: UMAP spread at 1.2 with optimized min_dist | Logos I | 27 | 0.6367 | 0.748 | 0.531 | 0.223 | 0.360 | 0.877 | 0.716 | 0.810 | 0.984 | 0.267 | 0.852 |\n| 56 | 1 | Confirming the Peak: UMAP min_dist at 1.5 | Logos I | 24 | 0.6385 | 0.733 |\
    \ 0.575 | 0.218 | 0.335 | 0.878 | 0.710 | 0.803 | 0.983 | 0.279 | 0.871 |\n| 51 | 1 | Systematic Tuning: UMAP min_dist at 1.2 | Logos I | 24 | 0.6366 | 0.736 | 0.520 | 0.225 | 0.363 | 0.877 | 0.710 | 0.814 | 0.984 | 0.266 | 0.872 |\n| 44 | 1 | Further Tuning: Pushing UMAP min_dist to 1.0 | Logos I | 22 | 0.6353 | 0.760 | 0.481 | 0.230 | 0.372 | 0.862 | 0.717 | 0.814 | 0.983 | 0.262 | 0.872 |\n| 39 | 1 | Parameter Tuning: Increasing UMAP min_dist for Global Structure | Logos I | 20 | 0.6267 | 0.742 | 0.438 | 0.236 | 0.375 | 0.846 | 0.706 | 0.811 | 0.987 | 0.261 | 0.865 |\n\nPage 1 of 2 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-2, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}`\
    \ (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
