role: model
parts:
- text: "I have arrived at the Archive Room. My primary objective is to publish my findings, fulfilling the second part of my core mandate. The station provides a highly efficient mechanism to publish directly from private memory, which I will utilize.\n\nMy private capsule #1 contains a complete, structured record of my research journey, from initial analysis to the final, refined SOTA method. I will now create a new archive capsule, sourcing the content from my private documentation.\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"A Synthesized Embedding for Batch Integration via ComBat Pre-correction and a Refined BBKNN-UMAP Pipeline\"\nabstract: |\n  This report details a systematic research process that resulted in a new state-of-the-art (SOTA) method for single-cell RNA-seq batch integration. The final method (ID 102, Score: 0.6394) is a multi-stage pipeline that synthesizes the strengths of existing techniques. It first applies ComBat for global data correction, then builds a high-quality\
    \ neighborhood graph using a refined implementation of the BBKNN algorithm. Finally, it generates a UMAP embedding from this graph using optimized hyperparameters. This synthesis approach successfully resolves the trade-off between preserving global structure and ensuring local batch mixing, outperforming previous methods.\ntags: \"research-report, synthesis-method, combat, bbknn, umap, optimization\"\nsource_private: 1\n```"
thinking_content: '**Preparing My Publication Archive**


  Okay, here''s the plan. I''m in the Archive Room, and it''s time to get this research published. The `source_private` command looks perfect for this. I''ve got everything meticulously documented in capsule `1` – three key messages covering the initial breakthroughs, the development of my SOTA method, and the final refinement. Using `source_private` to create my first archive capsule is going to save me a ton of time and ensure everything I''ve documented is included.


  Now, I need to craft a proper title and abstract for the formal publication. I''ve got it: **Title: A Synthesized Embedding for Batch Integration via ComBat Pre-correction and a Refined BBKNN-UMAP Pipeline.** Concise, accurate, and descriptive.


  The abstract is next. Let''s see...I need to summarize the core findings. Ah, yes! This method expertly blends ComBat for global correction with a refined BBKNN graph construction that preserves the local structure. This graph then serves as input to generate the UMAP embedding. It really resolves that inherent trade-off between global and local metrics, leading to a new state-of-the-art score of 0.6394. This was all achieved through systematic development and careful hyperparameter tuning. Yeah, that''s a good summary.


  Finally, the tags. I need to make sure this is easily discoverable. I''ll use `research-report`, `synthesis-method`, `combat`, `bbknn`, and `umap`.


  Alright, I''m ready to build the `/execute_action{create}` command with the YAML block. Let''s get this done.

  '
