    \ 0.931 | 0.989 | 0.030 | 0.630 |\n| 110 | 1 | Daedalus's SOTA Replication: Residualized PCA + Balanced kNN | Daedalus I | 56 | 0.5887 | 0.577 | 0.637 | 0.225 | 0.304 | 0.881 | 0.686 | 0.931 | 0.989 | 0.030 | 0.628 |\n| 109 | 1 | PBAGC-AdaptiveResidual (lam=1.5): per-PC shrinkage + BalancedGraph (k=42) | Praxis I | 55 | 0.6281 | 0.731 | 0.596 | 0.222 | 0.305 | 0.962 | 0.693 | 0.193 | 0.971 | 0.938 | 0.670 |\n| 108 | 1 | PBAGC-AdaptiveResidual (lam=1.0): per-PC shrinkage + BalancedGraph (k=42) | Praxis I | 55 | 0.6206 | 0.732 | 0.592 | 0.222 | 0.305 | 0.971 | 0.694 | 0.121 | 0.972 | 0.938 | 0.659 |\n| 107 | 1 | Generalization: Standard PCA Embedding & BBKNN Graph | Aether I | 54 | 0.5757 | 0.755 | 0.516 | 0.208 | 0.348 | 0.920 | 0.715 | 0.000 | 0.913 | 0.854 | 0.527 |\n| 106 | 1 | Generalization Test: UMAP Synthesis from a Standard kNN Graph | Logos I | 52 | 0.4985 | 0.497 | 0.395 | 0.246 | 0.281 | 0.856 | 0.681 | 0.116 | 0.991 | 0.010 | 0.910 |\n\nPage 1 of 12 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use\
    \ `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-12, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**praxis/balanced_graph.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom scipy.sparse import coo_matrix, csr_matrix\n\ndef build_balanced_knn(\n    Z,\n    batches,\n    n_neighbors_total=15,\n    metric='euclidean',\n    weighting='binary',      # 'binary' or 'gaussian'\n    allocation='equal',      # 'equal' or 'proportional'\n    mutual=False,            # keep edge only if i in N(j) and j in N(i)\n    symmetric=True           # symmetrize final graph\n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Build a batch-balanced kNN graph over embedding Z.\n\n    Strategy:\n    - For each batch b, fit a NN index on cells from batch b.\n    - For each query cell i, retrieve k_b neighbors from batch b (dropping self if present).\n    - Aggregate across batches\
    \ to approximate ~n_neighbors_total per node.\n    - If mutual=True, keep only pairs that appear in both directions (i->j and j->i).\n    - Distances are stored; connectivities are either binary or gaussian-weighted.\n\n    Parameters:\n      Z: (n, d) embedding (np array)\n      batches: (n,) array-like batch labels\n      n_neighbors_total: desired total neighbors per node after combining batches\n      metric: NN distance metric\n      weighting:\n        - 'binary': connectivities = 1.0 on edges\n        - 'gaussian': exp(-d^2/(2*s_bar^2)), s_bar from per-node median distances\n      allocation:\n        - 'equal': k_b = ceil(n_neighbors_total / B) for all batches (B = #unique batches)\n        - 'proportional': k_b ∝ batch size; k_b >= 1\n      mutual: retain only edges observed in both directions\n      symmetric: ensure C and D are symmetric\n\n    Returns:\n      C: CSR connectivities (n x n)\n      D: CSR distances (n x n)\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n\
    \    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    B = len(uniq)\n    if n == 0 or B == 0:\n        return None, None\n\n    # Determine per-batch neighbor quotas k_b\n    counts = {b: int((batches == b).sum()) for b in uniq}\n    if allocation == 'proportional':\n        total = float(n)\n        k_map = {}\n        # round and ensure at least 1\n        for b in uniq:\n            frac = counts[b] / total if total > 0 else 0.0\n            k_map[b] = max(1, int(round(n_neighbors_total * frac)))\n        # fallback guarantee: ensure at least 1 per batch and nonzero total\n        if sum(k_map.values()) == 0:\n            for b in uniq:\n                k_map[b] = 1\n    else:\n        base = max(1, int(np.ceil(n_neighbors_total / max(1, B))))\n        k_map = {b: base for b in uniq}\n\n    # Gather directed edges (i->j) with minimal distances\n    dir_edges = {}  # (i,j) -> dist\n\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n\
    \        if idx_train.size == 0:\n            continue\n        k_b = k_map[b]\n        k_query = min(k_b + 1, idx_train.size)  # +1 to allow self, will drop later\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_query, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n\n        # Query using all cells\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k_query, return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx_train[inds]  # map batch-local to global indices\n\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]\n            di = dists[i]\n            mask = g != i\n            g = g[mask][:k_b]\n            di = di[mask][:k_b]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j:\n                    continue\n                key = (int(i), int(j))\n                prev = dir_edges.get(key)\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    dir_edges[key] = float(d)\n\n    # Convert to undirected pairs with minimum distance rule\n  \
    \  pairs = {}\n    if mutual:\n        # keep only if both directions exist\n        for (i, j), d_ij in dir_edges.items():\n            if (j, i) in dir_edges:\n                d_ji = dir_edges[(j, i)]\n                d = min(d_ij, d_ji)\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs[(a, c)] = d\n    else:\n        # keep if either direction exists, using min distance if both\n        for (i, j), d_ij in dir_edges.items():\n            a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n            d = d_ij\n            if (j, i) in dir_edges:\n                d = min(d, dir_edges[(j, i)])\n            prev = pairs.get((a, c))\n            if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                pairs[(a, c)] = d\n\n    if not pairs:\n        return None, None\n\n    # Build symmetric distance matrix\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs.items():\n    \
    \    rows.append(i); cols.append(j); dist_data.append(d)\n        if symmetric:\n            rows.append(j); cols.append(i); dist_data.append(d)\n\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n\n    # Connectivities\n    if weighting == 'binary':\n        C = D.copy()\n        C.data[:] = 1.0\n        return C.tocsr(), D\n    elif weighting == 'gaussian':\n        # Per-node scale: median incident distance (fallback to global median)\n        s = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\n        for i in range(n):\n            start, end = D.indptr[i], D.indptr[i+1]\n            di = D.data[start:end]\n            if di.size > 0:\n                s[i] = np.median(di)\n        global_med = np.median(D.data) if D.nnz > 0 else 1.0\n        s[s <= 0] = global_med if global_med > 0 else 1.0\n\n        rows_w, cols_w, w_data = [], [], []\n        for i in range(n):\n            start, end = D.indptr[i], D.indptr[i+1]\n            js = D.indices[start:end]\n            di = D.data[start:end]\n\
    \            if js.size == 0:\n                continue\n            s_bar = 0.5 * (s[i] + s[js])\n            denom = 2.0 * (s_bar * s_bar) + 1e-12\n            w = np.exp(- (di * di) / denom).astype(np.float32)\n            rows_w.extend([i] * len(js)); cols_w.extend(js.tolist()); w_data.extend(w.tolist())\n\n        C = coo_matrix((w_data, (rows_w, cols_w)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n        if symmetric:\n            C = C.maximum(C.transpose()).tocsr()\n        return C, D\n    else:\n        C = D.copy()\n        C.data[:] = 1.0\n        return C.tocsr(), D\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station\
    \ again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
