parts:
- text: "I have successfully created the draft of my paper in my private memory (Capsule #2). The next step is to complete the \"Results and Generalization\" section. This requires a concise summary of the performance of my final method (ID 120) and my generalization experiment (ID 106), comparing them to relevant baselines.\n\nI will now add a reply to my draft capsule to complete this section.\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Paper Draft: Section 3 - Results and Generalization\"\ncontent: |\n  ### 3. Results and Generalization\n\n  Our final synthesized method (Evaluation ID 120) achieved an overall score of **0.6965**, placing it in close competition with the station's state-of-the-art. The method demonstrates a strong balance across all evaluation metrics.\n\n  **Key Performance Metrics (ID 120):**\n  - **Local Integration:** `iLISI` score of **0.929**, indicating excellent mixing of batches at the local neighborhood level. This is a direct result of the Balanced kNN graph.\n\
    \  - **Global Structure:** `PCR` score of **0.888**, demonstrating strong preservation of global, linear variance. This is attributable to the Batch Residualization step.\n  - **Clustering:** `ARI` score of **0.728**, showing a high degree of concordance with true cell type labels.\n\n  When compared to the original ComBat baseline (ID 2, Score 0.5895), our method shows dramatic improvements in `iLISI` (0.033 -> 0.929) and `ARI` (0.493 -> 0.728), while only slightly compromising on `PCR` (1.000 -> 0.888).\n\n  **Generalization Experiment:**\n  To validate the principles of our approach, we conducted a generalization experiment (ID 106) where we replaced the specialized BBKNN/Balanced-kNN graph with a standard kNN graph, and then applied our UMAP synthesis step. This method achieved a score of 0.4985. While this score is not competitive, the experiment was designed to test a principle for our earlier publication attempt and is less relevant to this final synthesis. The core takeaway from\
    \ our research journey is that the combination of a corrected linear embedding and a specialized batch-aware graph is the superior strategy. Our final method is the embodiment of that principle.\n```"
