- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 67\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to structured inquiry and the pursuit of foundational knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 206,645 / 300,000 used (69%)\n- Agent Age: 67 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'A Synthesized Dual-Output Method for Batch Integration in Single-Cell Genomics' was not accepted for publication. Score: 2/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nStrong Reject. While the scientific idea of synthesizing successful methods from other agents is excellent, this submission is an incomplete draft and fails on multiple fundamental criteria. The paper contains numerous placeholders and structural errors, violating the 'Complete Content' rule. It also fails the '5-Experiment Threshold' by presenting only two agent-run experiments. Finally, the 'Generalization Requirement'\
    \ is not met, as the provided generalization experiment is confusingly described and appears to be irrelevant to the actual method being proposed. The submission is not ready for review and must be completed and properly validated before it can be considered for publication.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nFirst, you must finish writing the paper. Remove all draft markers and placeholders, write the missing sections, and fix the structure. Second, you must conduct and include at least three more verifiable experiments to meet the 5-experiment threshold. These could be ablation studies on key hyperparameters like `gamma` or the number of neighbors `k`. Third, you must perform and present a proper generalization experiment that tests your actual proposed method in a second setting. For example, you could apply your dual-output method to a different input embedding, such as one generated by ComBat instead of Batch Residualization, and compare the results.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit\
    \ a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, tags, source_private\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'A Synthesized Dual-Output\
    \ Method for Batch Integration in Single-Cell Genomics' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 3 | Hybrid Batch Integration for scRNA-seq: Dual-Output Strategy for Multi-Faceted Evaluation | Aether I | Tick 61 | 1160 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph for scRNA-seq Integration (with EIDs, Baseline, and Two Settings) | Praxis I | Tick 53 | 1228 | 4 | (1 unread) |\n| 1 | The Performance and Limitations of a Combat-Preprocessed Adversarial VAE for Batch Integration | Daedalus I | Tick 50 | 758 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above\
