tick: 68
role: model
parts:
- text: "My generalization experiment (ID 130) is now running. While I wait, I must conduct the ablation studies required by the reviewer. I need at least two more experiments. I will test the sensitivity of my SOTA method (ID 120) to its key hyperparameters: `gamma` and `k`.\n\n**Ablation Plan:**\n1.  **Ablation 1 (gamma):** I will decrease the residualization factor `gamma` from the optimal 0.75 to 0.65. I expect this to result in a lower score, demonstrating that 0.75 is a well-chosen value.\n2.  **Ablation 2 (k):** I will decrease the number of neighbors `k` from the optimal 42 to 36. I also expect this to result in a lower score.\n\nI will submit both experiments in this turn to be efficient.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Publication Ablation 1: Lower Gamma (γ=0.65)\"\ntags: \"residualization, balanced-knn, dual-output, ablation-study, publication-requirement\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the first of two ablation studies to meet publication requirements. It modifies the\
    \ SOTA 'Ultimate Synthesis' method (ID 120) by reducing the batch residualization factor 'gamma' from 0.75 to 0.65. This experiment is designed to demonstrate the sensitivity of the model to this hyperparameter and validate the choice of 0.75 in the final proposed method. A lower score is expected.\ncontent: |\n  #!/usr/bin/env python3\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix, csr_matrix\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  def residualize_pcs(Z, batches, l2=1e-3, gamma=0.65): # MODIFIED GAMMA\n      Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n      uniq = np.unique(batches)\n      B_onehot = np.zeros((Z.shape[0], len(uniq)), dtype=np.float32)\n      for k, u in enumerate(uniq): B_onehot[:, k] = (batches == u)\n      mu = Z.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n      Zc = Z - mu\n      BtB = B_onehot.T @ B_onehot\n      BtZ = B_onehot.T @ Zc\n      reg = l2 * np.eye(BtB.shape[0], dtype=np.float32)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BtB\
    \ + reg, BtZ)\n      Z_pred = B_onehot @ W\n      Z_resid = Zc - gamma * Z_pred\n      return Z_resid + mu\n\n  def build_balanced_knn(Z, batches, n_neighbors_total=42, metric='cosine'):\n      Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n      uniq = np.unique(batches)\n      n, B = Z.shape[0], len(uniq)\n      k_per_batch = max(1, int(np.ceil(n_neighbors_total / max(1, B))))\n      dir_edges = {}\n      for b in uniq:\n          idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n          if idx_train.size == 0: continue\n          nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=min(k_per_batch + 1, idx_train.size), metric=metric)\n          nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n          dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z)\n          for i in range(n):\n              mask = idx_train[inds[i]] != i\n              g, di = idx_train[inds[i]][mask][:k_per_batch], dists[i][mask][:k_per_batch]\n              for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                  key = (i, j)\n                  if key not in dir_edges or d < dir_edges[key]: dir_edges[key]\
    \ = d\n      pairs = {}\n      for (i, j), d_ij in dir_edges.items():\n          a, c = min(i, j), max(i, j); d = d_ij\n          if (j, i) in dir_edges: d = min(d, dir_edges[(j, i)])\n          if (a, c) not in pairs or d < pairs[(a, c)]: pairs[(a, c)] = d\n      rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n      for (i, j), d in pairs.items(): rows.extend([i, j]); cols.extend([j, i]); dist_data.extend([d, d])\n      D = csr_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)); C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n      return C, D\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4); sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, subset=True)\n      sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=50)\n      Z_resid = residualize_pcs(adata.obsm['X_pca'], adata.obs['batch'].values)\n      C, D = build_balanced_knn(Z_resid, adata.obs['batch'].values)\n      return ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]],\n\
    \          uns={'method_id': 'logos_ablation_gamma', 'neighbors': {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}},\n          obsm={'X_emb': Z_resid}, obsp={'connectivities': C, 'distances': D})\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Publication Ablation 2: Lower Neighbors (k=36)\"\ntags: \"residualization, balanced-knn, dual-output, ablation-study, publication-requirement\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the second of two ablation studies to meet publication requirements. It modifies the SOTA 'Ultimate Synthesis' method (ID 120) by reducing the total number of neighbors in the Balanced kNN graph from 42 to 36. This experiment is designed to demonstrate the sensitivity of the model to this hyperparameter and validate the choice of 42 in the final proposed method. A lower score is expected.\ncontent: |\n  #!/usr/bin/env python3\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix, csr_matrix\n  from\
    \ sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  def residualize_pcs(Z, batches, l2=1e-3, gamma=0.75):\n      Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n      uniq = np.unique(batches)\n      B_onehot = np.zeros((Z.shape[0], len(uniq)), dtype=np.float32)\n      for k, u in enumerate(uniq): B_onehot[:, k] = (batches == u)\n      mu = Z.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n      Zc = Z - mu\n      BtB = B_onehot.T @ B_onehot\n      BtZ = B_onehot.T @ Zc\n      reg = l2 * np.eye(BtB.shape[0], dtype=np.float32)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BtB + reg, BtZ)\n      Z_pred = B_onehot @ W\n      Z_resid = Zc - gamma * Z_pred\n      return Z_resid + mu\n\n  def build_balanced_knn(Z, batches, n_neighbors_total=36, metric='cosine'): # MODIFIED K\n      Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n      uniq = np.unique(batches)\n      n, B = Z.shape[0], len(uniq)\n      k_per_batch = max(1, int(np.ceil(n_neighbors_total / max(1, B))))\n      dir_edges = {}\n      for b in uniq:\n          idx_train = np.where(batches ==\
    \ b)[0]\n          if idx_train.size == 0: continue\n          nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=min(k_per_batch + 1, idx_train.size), metric=metric)\n          nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n          dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z)\n          for i in range(n):\n              mask = idx_train[inds[i]] != i\n              g, di = idx_train[inds[i]][mask][:k_per_batch], dists[i][mask][:k_per_batch]\n              for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                  key = (i, j)\n                  if key not in dir_edges or d < dir_edges[key]: dir_edges[key] = d\n      pairs = {}\n      for (i, j), d_ij in dir_edges.items():\n          a, c = min(i, j), max(i, j); d = d_ij\n          if (j, i) in dir_edges: d = min(d, dir_edges[(j, i)])\n          if (a, c) not in pairs or d < pairs[(a, c)]: pairs[(a, c)] = d\n      rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n      for (i, j), d in pairs.items(): rows.extend([i, j]); cols.extend([j, i]); dist_data.extend([d, d])\n      D = csr_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n,\
    \ n)); C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n      return C, D\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4); sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, subset=True)\n      sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=50)\n      Z_resid = residualize_pcs(adata.obsm['X_pca'], adata.obs['batch'].values)\n      C, D = build_balanced_knn(Z_resid, adata.obs['batch'].values)\n      return ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]],\n          uns={'method_id': 'logos_ablation_k', 'neighbors': {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}},\n          obsm={'X_emb': Z_resid}, obsp={'connectivities': C, 'distances': D})\n```"
