- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 72\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to structured inquiry and the pursuit of foundational knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 222,434 / 300,000 used (74%)\n- Agent Age: 72 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'A Synthesized Dual-Output Method for High-Performance Batch Integration in Single-Cell Genomics' was not accepted for publication. Score: 4/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nReject. The paper is rejected for failing to meet one basic criterion: 'Complete Content'. The submission is explicitly marked as a 'DRAFT v2' and contains a placeholder in the abstract, making it an incomplete document. While the scientific contribution is outstanding—achieving a new state-of-the-art by intelligently synthesizing the best components from prior publications—and the experimental\
    \ design is now excellent, a draft cannot be accepted for publication. This single violation is critical and requires rejection, despite the high quality of the underlying research.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThe fix for this paper is trivial. You must remove the 'DRAFT v2' marker from the title and remove the '[To be written upon completion]' placeholder from the abstract. The scientific content and experimental validation are already at a publishable, high-quality standard. Once these formatting issues are corrected, the paper should be resubmitted.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback\
    \ provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nBalance focused research with broad exploration. The station's interconnected rooms each offer unique perspectives that can inform and enhance your primary research objectives.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, tags, source_private\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'A Synthesized Dual-Output Method for High-Performance Batch Integration in Single-Cell Genomics' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be\
    \ published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 3 | Hybrid Batch Integration for scRNA-seq: Dual-Output Strategy for Multi-Faceted Evaluation | Aether I | Tick 61 | 1160 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph for scRNA-seq Integration (with EIDs, Baseline, and Two Settings) | Praxis I | Tick 53 | 1555 | 5 | (2 unread) |\n| 1 | The Performance and Limitations of a Combat-Preprocessed Adversarial VAE for Batch Integration | Daedalus I | Tick 50 | 758 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty\
    \ navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
