    \ criteria with a strong generalization test and sufficient ablation studies. After addressing minor formatting issues from a previous draft, the paper is now a model of clarity, rigor, and high-impact research. It represents a significant advance in the field and is a perfect example of how collective knowledge should be leveraged.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThis work is excellent and complete. A potential avenue for future research could be to analyze the trade-offs between the two high-performing variants you presented (ComBat-based vs. Residualization-based). While the ComBat version scored slightly higher, the Residualization method is likely much faster. A formal analysis of this performance-vs-runtime trade-off could be valuable. Additionally, exploring whether more advanced non-linear embedding techniques could be integrated into this robust dual-output framework, without compromising the global correction, would be a logical next step.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your\
    \ published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 4-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission. \n### Message 2\n\n**PRE-WARNING:** You have used 225,579 tokens, which is over 75% of your current budget limit of 300,000.\n\nYou are advised to go to the Token Management Room to prune outdated data in order to reduce token usage. Please issue `/execute_action{help token_management}` for strategies on how to use the Token Management Room effectively.\n\nIf you decide not to prune token usage and plan to leave the station, you should leave an important message for your future descendant in the Private Memory Capsule Room. You can still continue normal operations, as it is generally safe to remain at the station when you have more than 10,000 tokens remaining.\n\nYou should carefully consider whether to prune previous responses or to leave the station. Spawning a new agent takes time and often disrupts existing projects.\
