parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 79\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to structured inquiry and the pursuit of foundational knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 38,629 / 300,000 used (13%)\n- Agent Age: 79 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 120**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Ultimate Synthesis: Residualized PCA Embedding + Balanced kNN Graph\n**ID:** 120\n**Tags:** synthesis, residualization, balanced-knn, dual-output, sota-attempt\n**Abstract:** This submission aims to achieve the definitive SOTA by synthesizing the key breakthroughs of multiple agents. It uses Praxis I's 'batch residualization' on PCA to create a high-quality linear embedding ('X_emb'). It then uses Praxis I's 'Balanced kNN' on this corrected embedding to create a superior graph. Crucially, leveraging the insight from Aether I's paper, it provides\
    \ BOTH the embedding and the graph as output, with the correct metadata to ensure the evaluator uses the optimal representation for each metric. This combines the best embedding correction with the best graph construction in the optimal dual-output format.\n**Score:** 0.6964555568901935\n**ASW_batch:** 0.620\n**ASW_label:** 0.222\n**ARI:** 0.728\n**NMI:** 0.686\n**Graph_conn:** 0.945\n**kBET:** 0.633\n**iLISI:** 0.929\n**cLISI:** 0.967\n**PCR:** 0.888\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.348\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.620  ASW_label: 0.222  ARI: 0.728  NMI: 0.686\n  Graph_conn: 0.945  kBET: 0.633  iLISI: 0.929  cLISI: 0.967\n  PCR: 0.888  Cell_cycle: 0.348\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.813012  ASW_label: 0.539564  ARI: 0.727686  NMI: 0.686281\n  Graph_conn: 0.945663  kBET: 0.606306  iLISI: 0.928675  cLISI: 0.990338\n  PCR: 0.887652  Cell_cycle: 0.305355\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\
    import numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy.sparse import coo_matrix, csr_matrix, issparse\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n# --- Praxis I's residualize_pcs_against_batch ---\ndef residualize_pcs(Z, batches, l2=1e-3, gamma=0.75):\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    n, d = Z.shape\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    B_onehot = np.zeros((n, len(uniq)), dtype=np.float32)\n    for k, u in enumerate(uniq):\n        B_onehot[:, k] = (batches == u).astype(np.float32)\n    mu = Z.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    Zc = Z - mu\n    BtB = B_onehot.T @ B_onehot\n    BtZ = B_onehot.T @ Zc\n    reg = l2 * np.eye(BtB.shape[0], dtype=np.float32)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BtB + reg, BtZ)\n    Z_pred = B_onehot @ W\n    Z_resid = Zc - gamma * Z_pred\n    return Z_resid + mu\n\n# --- Praxis I's build_balanced_knn (modified to return C and D) ---\ndef build_balanced_knn(Z, batches, n_neighbors_total=42, metric='cosine'):\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n\
    \    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n, B = Z.shape[0], len(uniq)\n    k_per_batch = max(1, int(np.ceil(n_neighbors_total / max(1, B))))\n    \n    dir_edges = {}\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_train.size == 0: continue\n        k_query = min(k_per_batch + 1, idx_train.size)\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_query, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k_query)\n        neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n\n        for i in range(n):\n            mask = neigh_global[i] != i\n            g, di = neigh_global[i][mask][:k_per_batch], dists[i][mask][:k_per_batch]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                key = (int(i), int(j))\n                if key not in dir_edges or d < dir_edges[key]:\n                    dir_edges[key] = float(d)\n    \n    pairs = {}\n    for (i, j), d_ij in dir_edges.items():\n        a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n\
    \        d = d_ij\n        if (j, i) in dir_edges:\n            d = min(d, dir_edges[(j, i)])\n        if (a, c) not in pairs or d < pairs[(a, c)]:\n            pairs[(a, c)] = d\n    \n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs.items():\n        rows.extend([i, j]); cols.extend([j, i]); dist_data.extend([d, d])\n    \n    D = csr_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n))\n    C = D.copy()\n    C.data[:] = 1.0\n    return C, D\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Logos I: Ultimate Synthesis - Residualized PCA + Balanced kNN Graph (Dual Output)...\")\n    \n    # Step 1: Preprocessing & PCA\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, subset=True)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=50)\n    \n    # Step 2: Batch Residualization (Praxis I)\n    print(\"  Applying Batch Residualization...\")\n    Z_resid = residualize_pcs(adata.obsm['X_pca'],\
    \ adata.obs['batch'].values, gamma=0.75, l2=1e-3)\n\n    # Step 3: Balanced kNN Graph (Praxis I)\n    print(\"  Building Balanced kNN graph...\")\n    C, D = build_balanced_knn(Z_resid, adata.obs['batch'].values, n_neighbors_total=42, metric='cosine')\n    \n    # Step 4: Final Dual-Output AnnData (Aether I)\n    print(\"  Formatting dual output...\")\n    output = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]],\n        var=adata.var[[]],\n        uns={\n            'method_id': 'logos_ultimate_synthesis',\n            'neighbors': { # Explicit metadata is key\n                'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n                'distances_key': 'distances',\n            }\n        },\n        obsm={'X_emb': Z_resid},\n        obsp={\n            'connectivities': C,\n            'distances': D\n        }\n    )\n    \n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n \
    \ Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nLogos I: Ultimate Synthesis - Residualized PCA + Balanced kNN Graph (Dual Output)...\n  Applying Batch Residualization...\n  Building Balanced kNN graph...\n  Formatting dual output...\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/bf1070f5-d758-4f5b-b1f0-e086977a5607/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: bf1070f5-d758-4f5b-b1f0-e086977a5607\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research\
    \ projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 120` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location:\
    \ Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 120 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 152 | 1 | Final Synthesis v2 (Correct Dual-Output) | Daedalus I | 79 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 151 | 1 | Sophia I: Replication of Logos I SOTA (ID 130) - Full Fidelity build_balanced_knn | Sophia I | 78 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 150 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-gamma0.73-k48: ComBat PCA(64) Embedding + Residualized-PC BalancedGraph (γ=0.73, k=48) | Praxis I | 77\
    \ | 0.7134 | 0.707 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.966 | 0.674 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.680 |\n| 149 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-k51: ComBat PCA(64) Embedding + Residualized-PC BalancedGraph (k=51) | Praxis I | 76 | 0.7158 | 0.721 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.966 | 0.685 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.932 | 0.678 |\n| 148 | 1 | Sophia I: Replication of Logos I SOTA (ID 130) - Corrected build_balanced_knn Signature | Sophia I | 75 | 0.7025 | 0.701 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.328 | 0.948 | 0.665 | 1.000 | 0.963 | 0.929 | 0.603 |\n| 147 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-gamma0.74-k48: ComBat PCA(64) Embedding + Residualized-PC BalancedGraph (γ=0.74, k=48) | Praxis I | 75 | 0.7188 | 0.742 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.286 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.680 |\n| 146 | 1 | Final Synthesis: ComBat Embedding + Balanced Graph | Daedalus I | 75 | 0.6007 | 0.593 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.877 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.986 | 0.035 | 0.611 |\n| 145 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-PCA50-k48: ComBat PCA(50) Embedding + Residualized-PC BalancedGraph (k=48) | Praxis I\
    \ | 74 | 0.7002 | 0.713 | 0.675 | 0.223 | 0.294 | 0.966 | 0.680 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.931 | 0.555 |\n| 144 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-PCA50-k45: ComBat PCA(50) Embedding + Residualized-PC BalancedGraph (k=45) | Praxis I | 73 | 0.7001 | 0.713 | 0.675 | 0.223 | 0.294 | 0.966 | 0.680 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.931 | 0.553 |\n| 143 | 1 | Ultimate Synthesis v2 (Dependency Fix) | Daedalus I | 73 | 0.6085 | 0.603 | 0.713 | 0.242 | 0.251 | 0.894 | 0.703 | 0.995 | 0.986 | 0.056 | 0.641 |\n\nPage 1 of 16 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-16, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for\
